{
  "source": "course-assets/training-bias/training-bias.mp4",
  "duration": 155.84,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.88,
      "text": "Let's say you ask three people a simple question."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.66,
      "end": 5.16,
      "text": "How much should I study for my exam?"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.08,
      "end": 8.0,
      "text": "Your science teacher says three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.54,
      "end": 11.1,
      "text": "Your mom says 30 minutes because you have to work tonight."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.62,
      "end": 14.0,
      "text": "And your best friend says studying is overrated."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.96,
      "end": 18.26,
      "text": "Three people you trust give you three completely different answers."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.0,
      "end": 23.3,
      "text": "That happens because each person brings their own specific life experience to the question."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.8,
      "end": 26.28,
      "text": "And that background naturally shapes the advice they offer."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.84,
      "end": 28.16,
      "text": "You heard three perspectives."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.16,
      "end": 31.28,
      "text": "Imagine an AI learned from only one."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.82,
      "end": 36.32,
      "text": "If a model scraped all of its study advice exclusively from websites written by science teachers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.66,
      "end": 38.64,
      "text": "it would internalize that three-hours rule."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.08,
      "end": 44.46,
      "text": "When you ask it how much to study, it spits out three hours, as if it is the absolute standard."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.82,
      "end": 46.08,
      "text": "That is training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.56,
      "end": 50.12,
      "text": "The model learned from sources that gave it only a narrow slice of reality."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.96,
      "end": 54.0,
      "text": "Let's look at this board detailing the types of training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.0,
      "end": 58.02,
      "text": "It shows us two distinct ways this problem creeps into AI outputs."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.9,
      "end": 62.92,
      "text": "The first mechanism is when a specific answer shows up too often in the data."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.46,
      "end": 68.26,
      "text": "Because our AI saw three hours repeated constantly across those teacher websites during its training phase,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.7,
      "end": 72.1,
      "text": "it learned to treat that as its go-to default response for everyone."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.98,
      "end": 75.52,
      "text": "The second mechanism is about what gets left out."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.94,
      "end": 79.52,
      "text": "Students who have to work evening shifts usually aren't the focus of those teacher websites."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.19999999999999,
      "end": 82.82,
      "text": "Because they are missing from the training data,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.32,
      "end": 86.94,
      "text": "the AI has almost no examples of their specific study habits."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.7,
      "end": 90.26,
      "text": "You can spot this happening in everyday interactions."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.88,
      "end": 94.06,
      "text": "Say you ask an AI to generate a list of successful entrepreneurs."
    },
    {
      "start": 94.76,
      "end": 96.12,
      "text": "It prints out 10 names."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.48,
      "end": 99.82,
      "text": "But as you read through them, you notice they are all tech founders."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.38,
      "end": 104.38,
      "text": "You look at that list and think, wait, why are all 10 in tech?"
    },
    {
      "start": 105.18,
      "end": 108.62,
      "text": "So you type a follow-up, asking who else would make the list"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.62,
      "end": 110.96,
      "text": "if we looked outside the technology sector."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.76,
      "end": 113.84,
      "text": "The list tells you which industry showed up."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.16,
      "end": 115.78,
      "text": "You'd need more evidence to know why."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.48,
      "end": 118.52,
      "text": "This graphic provides a three-step toolkit"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.52,
      "end": 120.42,
      "text": "for those moments when you suspect an answer"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.42,
      "end": 121.84,
      "text": "is shaped by training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.54,
      "end": 125.42,
      "text": "First, try asking, what's missing from this answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 126.12,
      "end": 127.7,
      "text": "Second, instruct the model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.16,
      "end": 130.2,
      "text": "show me examples that don't fit the pattern"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.2,
      "end": 130.86,
      "text": "you just gave."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.48,
      "end": 133.4,
      "text": "And third, tell it, answer again,"
    },
    {
      "start": 133.64,
      "end": 135.52,
      "text": "leaving out the most famous examples."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.52,
      "end": 140.28,
      "text": "These prompts are highly effective for interrogating the model, but they aren't magic."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.88,
      "end": 148.28,
      "text": "If the missing perspective simply wasn't included in the underlying training data, the AI cannot pull it out of thin air."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.08,
      "end": 151.42,
      "text": "AI learns from its training data."
    },
    {
      "start": 152.18,
      "end": 154.44,
      "text": "Bias in the data can shape the answer."
    }
  ],
